<article class="env-proposition" id="6AE167">
       
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/6AE167">Proposition <span data-tag="6AE167">4.3.1.5</span>.</a><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
Let $f: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ be a trivial fibration of simplicial sets. Then every diagram $\overline{p}: K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \calC $ is an $f$-colimit. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
Let $f: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ and $g: \calD \rightarrow \calE $ be inner fibrations of simplicial sets, and let $\overline{p}: K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \calC $ be a diagram. Suppose that $f \circ \overline{p}$ is a $g$-colimit. Then $\overline{p}$ is an $f$-colimit if and only if $\overline{p}$ is a $g \circ f$-colimit. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(3)$"><p>
Let $f: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ be an inner fibration of $\infty $-categories, and let $\overline{p}, \overline{q}: K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \calC $ be diagrams which are equivalent when viewed as objects of the $\infty $-category $\Fun (K^{\triangleright }, \calC )$. Then $\overline{p}$ is an $f$-colimit if and only if $\overline{q}$ is an $f$-colimit. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(4)$"><p>
Suppose given a Cartesian diagram 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { \calC ' \ar [d]^{f'} \ar [r]^{g} &amp;  \calC \ar [d]^{f} \\ \calD ' \ar [r] &amp;  \calD } \]
</div>
<p>
 of simplicial sets, where $f$ (and therefore also $f'$) is an inner fibration. Let $\overline{p}: K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \calC '$ be a diagram. If $g \circ \overline{p}$ is an $f$-colimit, then $\overline{p}$ is an $f'$-colimit. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
